0:["tAFgy3oTCENJzQlp2G2wa",[[["",{"children":[["slug","guide-to-a-northern-irish-accent","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__?{\"slug\":\"guide-to-a-northern-irish-accent\"}",{}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",{"children":[["slug","guide-to-a-northern-irish-accent","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__",{},[["$L1",[[["$","script","schema-0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2"}}],["$","script","schema-1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"@id\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/guide-to-a-northern-irish-accent#breadcrumb\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"News & Blog\",\"item\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/voiceover-news\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Guide to a Northern Irish Accent\",\"item\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/guide-to-a-northern-irish-accent\"}]}"}}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"Guide to a Northern Irish Accent"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header-sub","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$3"}}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"blog-post-body","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-main one-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>Listen to Northern Irish Celebrities</h2>\r\n<p>The first tip is to listen to as many Northern Irish celebrities’ voices as possible. Often, when we’re\r\nasked to do a regional accent, we’re really being asked to sound like a specific celebrity, so this is a\r\ngreat place to start. It also helps to have a specific impression in mind, instead of simply trying to do\r\nthe accent. Focusing on doing an impression of a famous Northern Irish actor or actress could give\r\nyou a way into the Northern Irish accent in general. Some well-known Northern Irish celebrities you\r\nmight like to listen to:<br>\r\n- Christine Blakely (TV presenter)<br>\r\n- Eamonn Holmes (TV presenter)<br>\r\n- Nadine Coyle (singer in Girls Aloud)<br>\r\n- Eddie Irvine (racing driver)<br>\r\n- Jamie Dornan (actor)<br>\r\n- Rory McIlroy (golfer)<br>\r\n- David Healy (footballer)<br>\r\n- Van Morrison (singer)<br>\r\n- Colin Murray (radio DJ)<br>\r\n- James Nesbitt (actor)<br>\r\n- Zöe Salmon (TV presenter)<br>\r\n- Liam Neeson (actor)<br>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n"}}],false,false]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-section two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/guide-to-a-northern-irish-accent.jpg","alt":"British voice over: Guide to a Northern Irish Accent","className":"blog-post-img"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>The R Sound in Northern Irish Accents</h2>\r\n<p>One of the aspects of the Northern Irish accent that sets it apart from many other UK accents is the\r\nletter R at the end of words. All Northern Irish accents (that’s right, there are lots!) use a\r\npronounced rhotic R on words that end with the letter R. Most English regional accents (with the\r\nexception of the West Country) do not say a rhotic R at the end of a word. If you can’t tell quite what\r\na rhotic R is, say the word ‘career’. The first R you come across in the word will be rhotic and the second might not be. In Northern Irish, both Rs are rhotic. So, if you want to say the word ‘car’, say\r\n‘career’ and take the ‘eer’ off the end.\r\nAnother way of capturing this sound is to say the letter R loudly and embrace your inner pirate. Say\r\n‘Arrr’ and really pronounce that R. Put a K in front of that pirate ‘arrr’ and you’re probably on the\r\nright track!\r\n</p>\r\n"}}]]}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"blog-post-section two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$4"}}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/guide-to-a-northern-irish-accent3.jpg","alt":"British voice over: Guide to a Northern Irish Accent","className":"blog-post-img"}]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"blog-post-section ","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>Need a British Male Voiceover?</h2>\r\n<p>If you're looking for a reliable <a href=\"/british-voiceover\" title=\"British Male Voiceover\">British voiceover artist</a> with 25+ years of experience, I’m happy to help. I don’t offer the Northern Irish accent, but I can turn around most UK regional styles or provide <a href=\"/character-voiceover\" title=\"Character Voice Demos\">character voiceovers</a> the same day. Let me know what you need voiced!</p>\r\n"}}],null]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-bottom-text","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$5"}}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-cta","children":["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/voiceover-news","className":"cta-btn cta-btn--outline","children":"← Back to News & Blog"}]}],["$","$L7",null,{"pageTitle":"Guide to a Northern Irish Accent","pageUrl":"guide-to-a-northern-irish-accent"}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"blog-related-strip","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-grid","children":[["$","$L6","876",{"href":"/tente-explainer-voiceover","className":"blog-related-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-img-wrap","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/tente-explainer-voiceover.jpg","alt":"tente-explainer-voiceover","className":"blog-related-img"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-title","children":"Happy Voiceover Style for TENTE"}]]}],["$","$L6","470",{"href":"/mi